package entity

import "sort"

// Effects are the closed catalogue of transformations a thing of the world can
// undergo. The catalogue is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH: the sensor selects an
// effect from it under a grammar (it physically cannot emit one that is not
// here), the choice is journaled, and each effect's mechanics — its committed
// condition, its fact sentence, whether it leaves a standing hazard, what means
// it needs — are DETERMINISTIC and live right here. This is the
// deterministic-core contract: the LLM classifies (which of these closed
// outcomes fits), the core computes (the outcome is fixed per key). Replaying
// the log re-applies the same mechanics from the journaled key — no LLM in the
// replay path. Open-endedness comes from a LARGE catalogue, not from free-form
// generation. Grow it by adding one row with its properties.

// Means an effect may require — a closed vocabulary the verdict engine checks
// against the instrument at hand (honest "нечем" when the means is absent).
const (
	MeansNone  = ""      // bare hands suffice
	MeansFire  = "огонь" // needs a flame / heat source (carried to the target)
	MeansWater = "вода"  // needs a water source (a river, a well, a barrel — splashed, not carried)
)

// IsMeans reports whether a value names a real elemental means — the shared
// vocabulary of the source axis (what a thing SUPPLIES, entity.SetSource) and an
// effect's requirement (what it NEEDS, Effect.Requires). MeansNone is not a means.
func IsMeans(s string) bool { return s == MeansFire || s == MeansWater }

// Effect keys are Russian infinitives — the grammar enum value AND the journaled
// key (events already carry Russian text; the morphology contract holds because
// the key never inflects, only the fact's gender-neutral verb does).
const (
	EffectBurn      = "поджечь"
	EffectChar      = "обуглить"
	EffectMelt      = "растопить"
	EffectExtingush = "потушить"
	EffectShatter   = "разбить"
	EffectBreak     = "сломать"
	EffectCrack     = "расколоть"
	EffectCrush     = "раздавить"
	EffectBend      = "погнуть"
	EffectPierce    = "проткнуть"
	EffectScratch   = "поцарапать"
	EffectTear      = "порвать"
	EffectCrumple   = "смять"
	EffectSoak      = "облить"
	EffectDry       = "высушить"
	EffectFreeze    = "заморозить"
	EffectStain     = "испачкать"
	EffectClean     = "отмыть"
	EffectPaint     = "покрасить"
	EffectTopple    = "опрокинуть"
	EffectFill      = "наполнить"
	EffectEmpty     = "опустошить"
	EffectBloody    = "окровавить"
)

// Effect is one entry of the catalogue.
type Effect struct {
	Key string
	// Fact is the deterministic outcome sentence with ONE %s for the entity's
	// name in the nominative. The verb is gender-neutral (3rd-person singular
	// present: «загорается», «трескается») so the name slots in without
	// agreement — the morphology contract.
	Fact string
	// Note is the committed condition text written onto the entity (closed
	// vocabulary; carried into knowledge packs so the world remembers).
	Note string
	// Hazard marks an effect that leaves a STANDING environmental threat (fire
	// keeps burning, endangers everyone present) — the tick floors fear on the
	// co-located so a burning place empties out.
	Hazard bool
	// Requires is the means the effect needs, or MeansNone. The verdict engine
	// refuses the deed honestly when the means is absent (unless MeansOptional).
	Requires string
	// MeansOptional marks an effect whose Requires means ENRICHES the outcome but is
	// not mandatory — the influence is achievable by an alternate means too. Putting
	// out a fire is the prototype: water (the means) leaves the thing wet and raises
	// steam, but smothering it (no water at hand) still works, leaving it merely cooled.
	// When the means is absent, the verdict proceeds with FactNoMeans instead of fizzling,
	// and the mutator skips the means' signature (the wetting). A hard-required means
	// (fire to ignite) is impotent when absent; an optional one only changes the outcome.
	MeansOptional bool
	// FactNoMeans is the outcome sentence for a MeansOptional effect performed WITHOUT
	// its means (the smother variant of extinguishing) — same one %s for the name. Empty
	// for effects whose means is mandatory (Fact always applies).
	FactNoMeans string
	// RequiresHazard marks an effect that only bites a thing CURRENTLY a standing
	// hazard — you cannot put out what is not alight. The verdict engine treats it
	// as impotent against a thing with no StateHazard, so it never overwrites a
	// settled condition (a charred ruin stays charred, not "extinguished").
	RequiresHazard bool
	// RequiresFlammable marks a catch-fire effect (burn, char) that only bites a
	// thing whose MATERIAL catches — the same per-thing judgment the spread uses
	// (Entity.CatchesFire). The verdict treats it as impotent against an
	// unflammable thing, so arson and spread share ONE flammability gate: a wooden
	// hut burns, a river or a clay mug does not, and ash never reignites.
	RequiresFlammable bool
	// RequiresFusible marks a MELT effect that only bites a thing whose THERMAL
	// response is FUSIBLE (плавится) — the heat twin of RequiresFlammable. The
	// verdict treats it as impotent against a thing that does not melt, so «растопить
	// камень факелом» fizzles: heat may char or do nothing, but stone never melts to
	// liquid. The affordance and the gate are one axis (thermal), as for fracture.
	RequiresFusible bool
	// RequiresVessel marks a CONTENTS effect (fill, empty) that only bites a thing whose
	// liquid FORM is a сосуд — a cavity that holds liquid. The verdict treats it as
	// impotent against a non-vessel, so «наполнить меч водой» fizzles: a blade has no
	// cavity to fill. The liquid-domain twin of RequiresFlammable/RequiresFusible.
	RequiresVessel bool
	// RequiresFull marks an effect (empty) that needs a vessel CURRENTLY holding liquid
	// — you cannot pour out an already-empty cup.
	RequiresFull bool
	// Content, when set, is the CONTENTS state this effect leaves: ContentFull (the
	// vessel is now full) or ContentEmpty (poured out). Empty leaves contents unchanged.
	Content string
	// ClearsHazard marks an effect that ENDS a standing hazard (extinguishing a
	// fire): the mutator drops the hazard markers, so the thing stops burning,
	// spreading and flooring fear. This is how a player fights a fire — the
	// counterpart to the tick's BurnOut, but the thing survives scorched, not
	// consumed.
	ClearsHazard bool
	// Integrity is the STRUCTURAL toll this effect inflicts — the level the thing's
	// condition is raised to (monotonically). IntegrityIntact (the zero value) means
	// no structural harm (a stain, a topple, a dousing): the thing is marked, not
	// weakened. Damaged things still function (a charred frame stands); Ruined ones
	// do not (shards, rubble). The world keys consequences to the level.
	Integrity Integrity
	// Moisture, when set, is the MOISTURE state this effect leaves: MoistureWet (the
	// thing is now wet — dousing, extinguishing-with-water) or MoistureDry (dried out).
	// Empty leaves moisture unchanged. Wet suppresses CatchesFire — water beats fire —
	// so a doused thing resists the spreading blaze until it dries (see moisture.go).
	Moisture string
	// Phase, when set, is the new physical FORM this effect leaves — the thing's
	// affordances (thermal, fracture) are RE-DERIVED to it, because they are properties
	// of a thing's STATE and this effect changed the state. Melting leaves a formless
	// puddle (heat-inert, no fracture); most effects change a thing's condition without
	// changing its form (a stain, a dent), so they leave Phase nil. The transition is
	// UNCONDITIONAL given the effect applied — its affordance gate (fusible for melt)
	// already ensured the effect only reaches a thing the transition suits.
	Phase *PhaseShift
}

// PhaseShift is the physical FORM a transforming effect leaves: the thermal response
// and fracture mode the thing has AFTER it. An empty axis means the new form has no
// response there (a formless puddle has no fracture), and ShiftPhase clears it.
type PhaseShift struct {
	Thermal  string
	Fracture string
}

